WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:05.059
So my husband left me three months ago for
his teenage secretary

00:00:05.059 --> 00:00:07.779
however, the other night he came home,

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:10.540
for some clean underwear and a fuck.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.560
Actually just for the underwear, I threw in
the fuck for free.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.500
You've probably already seen The Marvelous
Mrs. Maisel

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:21.100
after ordering books, paper towels or whatever
it is you buy on Amazon Prime.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:25.720
What are the fucking rules, I mean not the
fucking rules, the -fucking- rules?

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.600
Who gets first fucking rights?

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.440
A lot has already been made about the show's
depiction of a woman in a man's world.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:35.680
But just as important is the depiction of
a newborn New York counter-culture

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.120
that didn't want anything to do with the state.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.880
Those people just want to be left the fuck
alone.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.980
Maisel is a 1950s Upeer West Side New York
house wife

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:49.470
who discovers, after her husband leaves her,
that she has a knack for stand up comedy.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:52.240
Do you ever think you were supposed to be
something

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.740
and uh, and you suddenly realize you're not?

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:56.720
Yes, married.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:59.440
The domestic life she thought she wanted goes
up in smoke,

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:02.290
with nowhere to go, she stumbles into a East
Village theater

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.180
and tells us how she feels about it.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:10.200
Ignore this, ignore this, but imagine coming
home to these every night.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.160
Yeah!

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.780
Yeah they're pretty good, right?

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.780
Plus, they're standing up on their own.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.420
Shit.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.480
Quick trigger warning here for free speech
nerds.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.600
You're under arrest.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:26.480
What? Why?

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:29.240
Public indecency and performing without a
cabaret license.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.150
You need a license just to do that, seriously?

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:34.160
Yeah yeah you can bitch all about it to your
friend in the back seat there, go ahead.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.120
Hey.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:38.000
That's Lenny Bruce, he was a real 1950s comedian

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:41.580
who was routinely arrested for obscene jokes
he told on stage,

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.760
a topic he often worked into his act.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.560
As a comedian he just wanted to discuss taboo
ideas,

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:53.100
something his young, boundary-pushing audience
was into.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.740
Maisel is cut from the same cloth.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:57.020
That's the end of my show folks, join in next
week

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:00.320
when my grandmother steals my pearls and fucks
my boyfriend, five!

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.900
Even New Yorkers in the audience are on Maisel's
side

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:08.920
maybe that's because they felt the encroachment
of the state all around them

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.380
and they were sick of it too.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:15.680
Cities are made up of more than buildings
and roads, people make up a city.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:21.480
Jane Jacobs was a journalist and an urban
theorist in the 1950s

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.840
who pushed back on centrally planned city
developments

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.680
and huge, looming urban renewal projects.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:29.640
In the series, she and her followers protest
the building of a highway

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.160
through the middle  of a city park.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:37.320
Just that you are loud enough that Robert
Moses can hear you over his bulldozers!

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.780
She thought city planners shouldn't get to
decide what a city should be

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.200
but rather that people should be left alone
to live their lives

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:47.460
and let those choices determine how the community
would grow and function.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:55.480
After her husband bails, Maisel starts walking
into new worlds and trying on new identities

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.760
something she thinks she should be allowed
to do without anyone standing in the way

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.700
or literally dragging her off stage.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.460
In Maisel's day this was a new-ish idea, but
a good one.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:06.700
You said stuff to make a nun blush but you
didn't say it in a convent I'm assuming?

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.120
I was not in a convent.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.260
So where's the crime?

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:09.760
Right.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:13.800
Cops that hang around outside clubs, waiting
to harass entertainers for doing their thing,

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:16.100
I hate that, passionately.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:20.080
You start controlling speech, you're slip-sliding
toward fascism.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:20.740
Hello?

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.099
Perhaps the most individualistic theme in
the show

00:03:23.099 --> 00:03:26.370
is that Maisel doesn't even fall into the
second wave feminist category

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:28.410
history books associate with her time.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:33.069
Instead, her brand of feminism is less about
movement and more about personal choice.

00:03:33.069 --> 00:03:35.780
She enters and exits her corseted Upeer West
Side life

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:39.340
for the loose, pot smoking world of a downtown
comedy club whenever she sees fit.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:40.940
I thought you wanted to be a cool chick.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:44.660
I can be a cool chick with a doorman and a
Kelvinator Foodarama refrigerator, can't I?

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.240
Midge is building her own world,

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:51.160
it involves pearls, bright red lipstick, and
saying fuck a lot.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.599
And it's pretty fucked up to send in the cops
for that.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:57.060
The second season of The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel
is starting soon.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:59.060
Let's hope Midge can stay out of jail.

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:02.280
You've been a great audience ladies and gentlemen,
that's it for me,

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:05.780
my name is Mrs. Maisel, thank you and good
night!

